course: dictionary
lesson: 9930
title: The Taoiseach
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A title is a special name that tells you what job someone does. Taoiseach is a title, not a person's name. It is used for the leader of the government in the Republic of Ireland.
explain: «The Taoiseach is Ireland's head of government, like a prime minister.» Head of government means the person who leads the government. So a Taoiseach does a job like a prime minister in the UK.
explain: Be careful not to mix up two jobs. «Ireland has no king: its President lives in a big white house in a Dublin park and mostly does ceremonies, while the Taoiseach runs the government.» The President is the head of state, and the Taoiseach is the head of government.
explain: Context helps again. The sentence says the Taoiseach «answers to the Dáil», so the Dáil is the group the leader must answer to. Taoiseach is said TEE-shuck, and the Irish word itself means chief or leader.
fact: The Taoiseach is the prime minister of the Republic of Ireland.
fact: The Taoiseach is chosen by the Dáil, the main elected house of Ireland's Parliament.
fact: The Tánaiste is the deputy, the person who helps the Taoiseach.
fact: The President of Ireland is head of state, which is a different job from the Taoiseach's.
fact: In Irish, Taoiseach means "chief" or "leader", and it is said TEE-shuck.
exercise: What is the Taoiseach? | A king who lives in a big white house | A type of Irish dance | *The prime minister, the head of the government of Ireland | A park in Dublin
exercise: The President of Ireland mostly does what? | *Ceremonies, as head of state | Chooses the Dáil | Runs the government every day | Sings at the parliament
exercise: Which word means the deputy who helps the Taoiseach? | Dublin | *Tánaiste | Dáil | Taoiseach
test: «The Taoiseach runs the government and answers to the Dáil.» Who does the Taoiseach answer to? | *The Dáil | The President | A Dublin park | The Irish language
test: In Irish, what does Taoiseach mean? | *Chief or leader | A big white house | A parliament | A king
exam: Which statement is true? | *The Taoiseach leads the government, and the President is head of state | The Dáil is the name of a person | Ireland has a king who runs the government | The President runs the government, and the Taoiseach is head of state
